    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The bug has been fixed successfully. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command through the CLI wrapper was not passing the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate executable, so the GitHub Actions workflow file was not being created.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe Commander.js action handler was not receiving all the command-line arguments, including unknown options like `--ci`. The variadic args from the callback only contained parsed arguments, not unparsed options.\n\n## Solution\nInstead of relying on Commander's argument parsing, the fix extracts all arguments directly from `process.argv`, including everything after the `gate` command. This ensures all flags and arguments are passed through to frai-gate unchanged.\n\nThe key change in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-755):\n```typescript\n// Extract everything after 'gate' from argv\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst args = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\n```\n\n## Verification\nTested with: `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created (was missing before)\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`.",
